## Implementation

Commit: `d8cdd026c1ab78a62d49f4ea5083d66e5d12766a`
Header: `feat(storytime): add the tiles and the home card (track_id: storytime_app_rebuild_20261025)`

Changed files:

- `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/st/[level]/[week]/page.tsx`
- `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/layout.tsx`
- `apps/storytime/app/globals.css`
- `apps/storytime/messages/en.json`
- `apps/storytime/messages/th.json`

Behavior:

- The home view shows the read-along, decodable, and song tiles. Each tile has a picture
  with `alt = image.caption`. A karaoke tile shows only when `song.karaoke` exists.
- Only recorded files play. The tile labels and the home words read an app naming table
  (`TILE_LABEL_AUDIO`, `HOME_WORD_AUDIO`). The sound of the week reads `focus.element.audio`.
  The tables are empty until production delivers the files, so a missing recording shows no
  speaker. The page never calls `speechSynthesis` and holds no `home.words` audio field.
- The Thai parent line comes from `home.line.th` and is omitted when empty. The three home
  words come from `home.words`. The frame comes from `focus.frame`. The activity comes from
  `home.activity`. Thai text has `lang="th"`; English text has `lang="en"`.
- Entry tiles have `min-h-16`. Speaker controls have `min-h-16 min-w-16` (64 px). The measured
  browser part of AC-5.2 in portrait and landscape stays with the browser gate of task 3.7.
- Sarabun loads through `next/font/google` in the locale layout. next/font self-hosts the font,
  so the browser makes no request to a font provider, and the app adds no dependency.
  `app/globals.css` sets `--font-sans` from `--font-sarabun`.
- `en.json` and `th.json` hold the same ten flat keys, and every Thai value is non-empty.

